{"id": "EUVD-2026-94389", "enisaUuid": "a3f234b4-38fb-3045-9bde-dadcc8c529e1", "description": "ImageMagick is free and open-source software used for editing and manipulating digital images. Prior to 7.1.2-32, an unauthenticated adjacent-network client can repeatedly connect to the distributed pixel cache server and exhaust its available connections, causing denial of service. This issue is fixed in version 7.1.2-32.", "datePublished": "2026-10-07T15:26:37", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-07T17:06:45", "baseScore": 4.3, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:A/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:L", "references": ["https://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick/security/advisories/GHSA-2vwg-3g4g-qprm", "https://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick/commit/cafc7372c8113a9636766f0eddde7b90373c9b44", "https://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick/releases/tag/7.1.2-32"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-106570"], "assigner": "GitHub_M", "epss": 0.22, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "a35dd113-0318-396b-9760-592e5d44b9d5", "product": {"name": "ImageMagick", "vendor": {"name": "ImageMagick"}}, "product_version": "< 7.1.2-32"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "6674c5c5-37e5-3829-8010-a32c45a144c1", "vendor": {"name": "ImageMagick"}}], "isExploited": false}